-- title:
--   Base change of the level-N₀ special-fibre dictionary
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N_0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and write $X_0 =$ `DRLevel.toBase0 N₀ q`$\colon X_0(N_0) \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{DRLevel.R}\,q)$ for the Igusa structure morphism $\mathrm{igusaTo}\,N_0\,q$. Let $\kappa_0$ be a field with a ring homomorphism $t_0 \colon$ `DRLevel.R q` $\to \kappa_0$, and suppose given a `CurveModel` $M_0$ over $\kappa_0$ for the intermediate field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa_0\,N_0 = \kappa_0(\mathrm{jqModC}, \mathrm{jqNModC})$ inside $\kappa_0((q))$ — that is, an integral scheme $M_0.C$ proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa_0$, a ring isomorphism of that field with the function field of $M_0.C$ compatible with the base field, and a bijection of closed points with places matching stalks to valuation rings — together with a morphism $e_0 \colon M_0.C \to$ `DRLevel.fibre0 t₀` $= X_0(N_0) \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R_q} \operatorname{Spec}\kappa_0$ that is an isomorphism, such that: the preimage under $e_0$ followed by the first projection of the open image of `IgusaScheme.ιFin N₀ q` is non-empty; $e_0$ followed by the second projection is $M_0.\mathrm{toBase}$; and for every $b$ in the subalgebra `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin N₀ q` of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,N_0$, the element $\mathrm{read}\,b \in \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa_0\,N_0$ obtained by transporting $b$ through the global-sections isomorphisms of the chart, pulling back along $e_0$ followed by the first projection, taking the germ in the function field and applying $M_0.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, satisfies: $\mathrm{read}\,b = \mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa_0\,N_0$ whenever $b =$ `IgusaScheme.jChartFin N₀ q`, and $\mathrm{read}\,b = \mathrm{jNGeomGen}\,\kappa_0\,N_0$ whenever the Laurent series underlying $b$ equals $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,N_0\,j_q$. Then for every algebraically closed field $\kappa$, every $t \colon$ `DRLevel.R q` $\to \kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon \kappa_0 \to \kappa$ with $\varphi \circ t_0 = t$, there exist a `CurveModel` $M$ over $\kappa$ for $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,N_0$ and an isomorphism $e \colon M.C \to$ `DRLevel.fibre0 t` with non-empty chart preimage, with $e$ followed by the second projection equal to $M.\mathrm{toBase}$, and satisfying the same two conditions on the readings of the elements of `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin N₀ q`, now with $\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,N_0$ and $\mathrm{jNGeomGen}\,\kappa\,N_0$.
--
--   This is the transport statement, along a change of geometric point $\varphi \colon \kappa_0 \to \kappa$ into an algebraically closed field, of the level-$N_0$ dictionary identifying the special fibre of the Igusa scheme $X_0(N_0)$ with a smooth proper model of the field generated by the two modular $j$-functions, the chart generators being read as those functions. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_curveModel_iso_fibre0_chartPin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_curveModel_iso_fibre0_chartPin) to pass from the dictionary over a residue field to the dictionary over an arbitrary algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$.
